    "Dynamic MAT/TRC/GRF parity tests rule out a conversion-introduced axis, side, sign or timestamp error for the checked columns. They do not prove physical correctness of the source acquisition or contact model.",
    "AB06 historical static times are dilated twofold, but pose and marker rows remain aligned and numerically preserved. Median static ground registration uses poses without velocity/time weighting; the clock discrepancy alone does not demonstrate an effect on paired dynamics.",
    "The AB07 ankle IK changes indirectly by about +5.10 degrees after preparation. This is a real preparation effect, not proof of an error or unique explanation for the +40% load difference.",
    "Both primary windows have original Speed=0.5 and subject-specific measured forces/body weights. Source data checks alone cannot separate intrinsic anatomy from prosthesis fitting, marker calibration, reference/governor effects or contact geometry."
